  "term": "self-transcendence",
  "definition": "In the history of empirical research, self-transcendence refers to going beyond the self’s boundaries across dimensions such as the physical and social, often also encompassing broader prosocial, spiritual, or religious outlooks and related psychological and behavioral qualities. Historically, major measures in nursing and psychobiology have framed it as a final stage of human psychological development and adaptability, especially in later life.",
